        "locator": {
          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "479d3c40-0d70-58cb-a69a-70f8da6e91a1",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 591,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.050:block:1",
          "start": 210
        },
        "quote": "(1) An as-graded grading plan prepared by the civil engineer, including original ground surface elevations, as-graded ground surface elevations, lot drainage patterns and locations and elevations of all surface and subsurface drainage facilities. The civil engineer shall state that to the best of his knowledge the work was done in accordance with the final approved grading plan.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.050:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 17.05.050 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "40c4ee1a-7ba1-590f-9524-6f0c920e78b0",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1048,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.050:block:2",
          "start": 592
        },
        "quote": "(2) A soils grading report prepared by the soils engineer, including locations and elevations of field density tests, summaries of field density tests, summaries of field and laboratory tests and other substantiating data and comments on any changes made during grading and their effect on the recommendations made in the soils engineering investigation report. The soils engineer shall render a finding as to the adequacy of the site for the intended use.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.050:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 17.05.050 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "83a5a1c4-e892-58a5-9ed5-529e9f3b2cec",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1462,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.050:block:3",
          "start": 1049
        },
        "quote": "(3) A geologic grading report prepared by the engineering geologist, including a final description of the geology of the site and any new information disclosed during the grading and the effect of such new information on recommendations incorporated in the approved grading plan. The engineering geologist shall render a finding as to the adequacy of the site for the intended use as affected by geologic factors.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.050:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 17.05.050 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "b7005a11-79d3-578f-9713-a93f36d9ed3f",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1945,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.05.050:block:4",
          "start": 1463
        },
        "quote": "(b) Notification of Completion. The permit holder shall notify the Development Coordination Office when the grading operation is ready for final inspection. Final approval shall not be given until all work, including installation of all drainage facilities and their protective devices, and all erosion control measures have been completed in accordance with the final approved grading plan and the required reports have been submitted. (Ord. 16432 § 8, 3-10-92. Code 1995 § 66-90.)",
